WEBVTT

S01
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.922
NeuroSphere is a customer-hosted governance layer for AI agents. This video walks through it using a synthetic sandbox, so everything you see is generated data.

S02
00:00:11.922 --> 00:00:27.654
The sandbox is isolated from real data. When sandbox mode is switched on, a banner stays on screen so you always know you are looking at synthetic content. Real ingestion is a separate path, and the demo never uses production data.

S03
00:00:28.654 --> 00:00:48.625
A viewer browses the synthetic estate: the map, the recommendations and the catalog. The sandbox injects a cost spike, with token use raised twelve times and volume three times in a known window, but the local dashboard does not draw it. The viewer can read, and the service refuses changes.

S04
00:00:49.625 --> 00:01:01.547
An analyst investigates a seeded latency regression, replays a trace through an affected agent, and runs a saved report. Reports run under the analyst's own scope on every run.

S05
00:01:02.547 --> 00:01:23.613
A steward reviews consolidation candidates and unused agents. Candidates are always labelled as candidates and are never merged automatically. The action executor rechecks permission, honors approvals, records an audit entry and verifies the real change. In the seeded demo, decisions stop before execution.

S06
00:01:24.613 --> 00:01:41.549
An admin works with deliberately messy synthetic input: duplicate, out of order and malformed events. Quarantine and replay let the admin compare what was injected with what the pipeline accepted. Admin is a scoped role, with no unrestricted bypass.

S07
00:01:42.549 --> 00:01:55.921
An auditor reads the audit trail. Each action records who acted, the target and version, and the outcome. The data is synthetic, so none of this is evidence of compliance or authorization.

S08
00:01:56.921 --> 00:02:19.066
Support for Azure Government is gated by a capability matrix, and unsupported combinations are disabled rather than hidden. Availability, general availability and authorization are separate questions, and this video makes no claim about any of them. Dashboard and map speeds in the product documents are planning targets, not measured promises.
